    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nProblem:\nI will take the example of {} to explain.\nRight now, in mini.ai search is first done on current line. This leads `vi{` to select next pair of `{}` if both are on same line, even if cursor is inside another `{}`, even in `cover_or_next` mode.\n \nCurrent Workarounds:\nI can set `['{']` to false in `custom_textobjects` but then I can't use n or l with that.\nI can set the `search_method` to `cover` but then, I need to use n almost every time, which is a little annoying.\n\nFeature Request:\nI am therefore requesting a new `search_method` with search behaviour exactly like native vim.\ni.e. select surrounding `{}` if inside `{}` and next '{}' if not inside irrespective of what is on current line.\nOr any equivalent solution that addresses this problem would be greatly appreciated. ",
