        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I can see all issues with similar requests are getting marked duplicate/not planned, but I think these suggestions are still important.\n\nI don't think I can add more to what was already said about it.\n\nThe main reason for existing `cover_or_next` \"two stage\" behavior is because the default one was confusing enough for me to want to first prioritize current line textobjects/surroundings over any multi-line ones. However, if done today, I'd do the `cover` behavior as default and suggest using next/last variants explicitly (this is what I've been doing myself for several years now).",
